---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const { names } = Astro.props as { names: Record<string, string> };
const base = '/participation-estimated-coalitions/20261107-03/';
type Values = { returning_count: number; reported_switcher_count: number; apparent_absence_count: number;
	reported_switchers_pct_of_original_coalition: number; apparent_absence_pct_of_original_coalition: number;
	infeasible_as_closed_original_coalition: boolean };
type Composition = { conditional_current_electorate_count: number;
	reported_share_pct_of_current_electorate: number; reported_current_choice_counts: Record<string, number | null> };
type Comparison = { state_code: string; contest_code: string; reference: Record<string, Values>;
	preliminary_turnout: { ballots: number; native_national_ballots: number };
	official_2024_baseline: Record<string, number>; current_electorate_composition: Record<string, Composition>;
	sensitivity_scenarios: { coalitions: Record<string, Values> | null }[] };
type Jurisdiction = { state_code: string; preliminary_turnout: { ballots: number }; conditional_contests: string[];
	all_voter_joint_table_dispositions: { contest_code: string; status: string }[] };
const review: { state_comparisons: Comparison[]; national_house_comparison: Comparison;
	jurisdictions: Jurisdiction[] } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}estimated-coalition-scenarios.json`, 'utf8'));
const integer = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
const count = (value: number) => integer(Math.round(value / 1000) * 1000);
const flow = (value: number | null) => value === null ? 'Unavailable' : count(value);
const pct = (value: number) => `${value.toFixed(1)}%`;
const office: Record<string, string> = { SG: 'Senate', GG: 'Governor', HG: 'House' };
const name = (row: Comparison) => `${row.state_code === 'US' ? 'United States' : names[row.state_code]} / ${office[row.contest_code]}`;
const range = (row: Comparison, prior: string) => {
	const values = row.sensitivity_scenarios.flatMap(scenario => scenario.coalitions
		? [scenario.coalitions[prior].apparent_absence_pct_of_original_coalition] : []);
	return `${pct(Math.min(...values))}–${pct(Math.max(...values))}`;
};
const groups = [
	{ label: 'National House — 50 states, D.C. excluded', rows: [review.national_house_comparison], open: true },
	{ label: 'State Senate and governor — 61 separate comparisons', rows: review.state_comparisons, open: false },
];
const states = new Set(review.state_comparisons.map(row => row.state_code)).size;
---

<section id="participation-estimated-coalitions" aria-labelledby="estimated-coalitions-title">
	<h3 id="estimated-coalitions-title">Preliminary estimates across states</h3>
	<p><strong>{states} states · {review.state_comparisons.length} separate contests, plus national House.</strong>
		This separate tier scales qualified joint survey tables to UF Election Lab's preliminary turnout
		estimates. Every source numerator is labeled <strong>Initial Estimate</strong>, not an official
		observed or certified count. The reported-count snapshots below remain separate.</p>
	<p><strong>Apparent absence is not measured staying home.</strong> It includes migration, mortality,
		recall and population-estimation error. The reference assumes each contest's recalled-choice
		composition represents all ballot-casters; exact response selection remains unverified.
		Some current choices were retained from pre-election interviews after unsuccessful recontact.</p>
	{groups.map(group => <details class="explorer-notes" open={group.open}>
		<summary>{group.label}</summary>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${group.label}: original coalitions`}>
			<table><caption>Scenario counts rounded to 1,000. Percentages use the original 2024 coalition.
				Rounded zero does not establish no switching. Never add offices or national/state comparisons.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">2026 comparison</th><th scope="col">2024 coalition</th>
					<th scope="col">Official 2024 votes</th><th scope="col">Estimated returning</th>
					<th scope="col">Reported opposite-party choice</th><th scope="col">Apparent absence</th>
					<th scope="col">Absence sensitivity<br />(not a confidence interval)</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{group.rows.flatMap(row => ['R', 'D'].map(prior => {
					const value = row.reference[prior];
					return <tr data-estimated-state={row.state_code} data-estimated-contest={row.contest_code} data-estimated-prior={prior}>
						<th scope="row">{name(row)}<br /><small>Preliminary estimated total</small></th>
						<td>{prior === 'R' ? 'Trump' : 'Harris'}</td>
						<td>{integer(row.official_2024_baseline[prior])}</td>
						<td>{count(value.returning_count)}</td>
						<td>{count(value.reported_switcher_count)}<br />{pct(value.reported_switchers_pct_of_original_coalition)}</td>
						<td>{count(value.apparent_absence_count)}<br />{pct(value.apparent_absence_pct_of_original_coalition)}
							{value.infeasible_as_closed_original_coalition && <><br />Incompatible with a closed original coalition</>}</td>
						<td>{range(row, prior)}</td>
					</tr>;
				}))}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<h4>Recalled prior nonvote and other presidential choice</h4>
		<p>These are estimated composition counts of the current electorate, not first-time-voter,
			eligibility-entry or demographic turnout rates. A reported presidential nonvoter may have
			voted in another 2024 contest. Suppressed current-choice cells remain unavailable.</p>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${group.label}: prior presidential composition`}>
			<table><caption>Composition count = estimated total × published recalled-choice share.
				Choice counts additionally multiply by the published conditional choice; no suppressed values are reconstructed.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">2026 comparison</th><th scope="col">No 2024 presidential vote</th>
					<th scope="col">2026 D / R from that group</th><th scope="col">Other 2024 presidential choice</th>
					<th scope="col">2026 D / R from that group</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{group.rows.map(row => {
					const n = row.current_electorate_composition.N;
					const o = row.current_electorate_composition.O;
					return <tr data-estimated-composition-state={row.state_code} data-estimated-composition-contest={row.contest_code}>
						<th scope="row">{name(row)}</th>
						<td data-estimated-nonvote>{count(n.conditional_current_electorate_count)}<br />{pct(n.reported_share_pct_of_current_electorate)}</td>
						<td data-estimated-nonvote-flows>{flow(n.reported_current_choice_counts.D)} / {flow(n.reported_current_choice_counts.R)}</td>
						<td>{count(o.conditional_current_electorate_count)}<br />{pct(o.reported_share_pct_of_current_electorate)}</td>
						<td>{flow(o.reported_current_choice_counts.D)} / {flow(o.reported_current_choice_counts.R)}</td>
					</tr>;
				})}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>)}
	<p class="caption">Returning = N26 × q; reported opposite-party choices = N26 × q × p;
		apparent absence = T24 − N26 × q. The sensitivity varies estimated totals by −5%, 0 and +5%
		and transfers −2, 0 or +2 recalled-composition points from Harris to Trump. These are stress
		assumptions, not probability intervals or estimated missing ballots. Composition is not renormalized.</p>
	<p>The national House comparison excludes D.C. from both 2024 coalitions and 2026 estimated totals
		because SSRS did not sample it. Its 50-state population estimate is
		{integer(review.national_house_comparison.preliminary_turnout.ballots)}, not the native
		51-jurisdiction total. This is matched-scope aggregation, not allocation to states.</p>
	<p>This version uses the November 7 source snapshot. All 61 supported state-contest estimates
		are unchanged; the national estimate and Washington's ballot-total coverage row are revised.
		Other demographic and age panels retain their separately dated, frozen inputs and are not
		silently recalculated with this newer total.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Estimated-total coverage: all 50 states and D.C.</summary>
		<p>Every jurisdiction has its own preliminary numerator. Missing qualified joint evidence is not zero.</p>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Nationwide estimated-total scenario coverage">
			<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Jurisdiction</th><th scope="col">Preliminary estimated ballots</th>
				<th scope="col">Qualified comparisons / next evidence</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{review.jurisdictions.map(row => <tr data-estimated-coverage={row.state_code}>
					<th scope="row">{names[row.state_code]}</th><td>{integer(row.preliminary_turnout.ballots)}<br />Initial Estimate</td>
					<td>{row.conditional_contests.length ? row.conditional_contests.map(code => office[code]).join(', ')
						: 'Acquire applicable qualified state-specific joint choice evidence; no national allocation'}
						{!row.conditional_contests.length && row.all_voter_joint_table_dispositions.length > 0 &&
							<><br /><small>{row.all_voter_joint_table_dispositions.map(item => `${office[item.contest_code] ?? item.contest_code}: ${item.status}`).join('; ')}</small></>}
					</td>
				</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Source versions, attribution and limitations</summary>
		<p>Michael McDonald, University of Florida Election Lab, CSV v0.2 and documentation v0.1,
			licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0. All 51 state/D.C. estimates sum to the
			CSV's {integer(review.national_house_comparison.preliminary_turnout.native_national_ballots)}
			national estimate. This snapshot's CSV HTTP Last-Modified is November 7, 2026 at 02:35:29 GMT;
			that is not an inferred webpage update time.</p>
		<p>The earlier, frozen definition review and its separate page clocks remain in the download,
			explicitly distinguished from this refreshed CSV. The native page defines estimated total ballots, not votes
			for governor or senator; the older codebook still leaves this field's documentation as TBD.
			The publisher notes substantial incomplete-reporting uncertainty, particularly California and Washington.</p>
		<p>The ZIP contains full unchanged licensed turnout data/documentation, source receipts, the official
			FEC workbook, permitted selected joint survey inputs, exact code, tests and outputs.
			No demographic/county/precinct allocation, causal persuasion or share-of-overall-swing estimate
			is released. No individual records or restricted NORC materials are included.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete preliminary estimates + licensed inputs + code (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}estimated-coalition-scenarios.json`} download>Exact preliminary counts + composition + sensitivity (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Preliminary archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
		<a href="/participation-estimated-coalitions/20261107-02/complete-analysis.zip" download>Previous complete version (ZIP)</a>
		<a href="https://election.lab.ufl.edu/dataset/2026-general-election-turnout-rates-v0-2/">UF source and documentation</a>
		<a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0 license</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-estimated-coalitions { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
